From: hashtagbasit <53941105+hashtagbasit@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] input: retroid: trigger travel from the fixed rest reading

The MCU reports each trigger counting down from 0x610 at rest.
trigger_left_max / trigger_right_max start at that value but are also the
reported evdev range that calibration rewrites, and the sample was taken
from them. After a calibration every sample moved by the correction, so a
full press no longer reached the top of the range, and calibrating again
made it worse. Measure from the fixed rest reading; the parameters stay
the reported range only.

--- a/drivers/input/joystick/retroid.c	2026-10-10 02:07:01
+++ b/drivers/input/joystick/retroid.c	2026-10-10 02:07:18
@@ -64,11 +64,18 @@
 
 static int update_params=0;
 
-static int trigger_left_max=0x610;
+/*
+ * Raw MCU reading with the trigger released. The samples count down from
+ * here as the trigger is pressed; trigger_*_max below is only the reported
+ * range, which calibration changes.
+ */
+#define RETROID_TRIGGER_REST 0x610
+
+static int trigger_left_max=RETROID_TRIGGER_REST;
 static int trigger_left_deadzone=0x0;
 static int trigger_left_antideadzone=0x0;
 
-static int trigger_right_max=0x610;
+static int trigger_right_max=RETROID_TRIGGER_REST;
 static int trigger_right_deadzone=0x0;
 static int trigger_right_antideadzone=0x0;
 
@@ -245,11 +252,11 @@
 
 	int16_t value;
 
-	value = (int16_t)(trigger_left_max - (data->data[2] | (data->data[3] << 8)));
+	value = (int16_t)(RETROID_TRIGGER_REST - (data->data[2] | (data->data[3] << 8)));
 	input_report_abs(indev, ABS_HAT2X,
 			 ( value < trigger_left_deadzone )? 0 : value - trigger_left_antideadzone);
 
-	value = (int16_t)(trigger_right_max - (data->data[4] | (data->data[5] << 8)));
+	value = (int16_t)(RETROID_TRIGGER_REST - (data->data[4] | (data->data[5] << 8)));
 	input_report_abs(indev, ABS_HAT2Y,
 			 ( value < trigger_right_deadzone )? 0 : value - trigger_right_antideadzone);
 
